### ============================================
### PASSWORD RESET ENDPOINTS
### ============================================
### Base URL: http://localhost:29000/api/v1/password
### Rate Limits: 3/hour (forgot), 10/hour (verify), 5/hour (reset)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:29000
@passwordPath = /api/v1/password

### ============================================
### PASSWORD RESET FLOW (EMAIL OR SMS)
### ============================================
### Flow:
### 1. If user's email is verified → sends email verification code
### 2. If user's email is NOT verified → sends SMS verification code (following signup workflow)
###    - Telegram Gateway (if X-Telegram-Account header is "true")
###    - Flash Call (if Android device)
###    - SMS (if iOS/Web device)

### 1. Request Password Reset
### Rate Limit: 3 requests/hour per IP
### Note: Always returns success to prevent user enumeration
### Flow: Finds user by phone number, checks if email is verified, sends email or SMS code accordingly
POST {{baseUrl}}{{passwordPath}}/forgot
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Type: Android
X-Telegram-Account: false
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.data) {
        client.log("Verification method: " + response.body.data.verificationMethod);
        client.log("Verification type: " + response.body.data.verificationType);
    }
%}

### 2. Verify Code and Get Reset Token
### Rate Limit: 10 requests/hour per IP
### Note: User must provide phone number and the verification code (email or SMS, depending on user's email verification status)
POST {{baseUrl}}{{passwordPath}}/verify-code
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890",
  "code": "1234"
}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200 && response.body.data) {
        client.global.set("resetToken", response.body.data.resetToken);
    }
%}

### 3. Reset Password Using Reset Token
### Rate Limit: 5 requests/hour per IP
POST {{baseUrl}}{{passwordPath}}/reset
Content-Type: application/json
X-Device-Id: device-12345
X-Forwarded-For: 192.168.1.1

{
  "resetToken": "{{resetToken}}",
  "newPassword": "***REMOVED***",
  "confirmPassword": "***REMOVED***"
}

